 organic growth  changes in strange ways these are very  strange  what  well they're also different to look at  them you wouldn't say that they're the  things be seized the girl from the same  branch structure and they held strange  colors that could not be put into any  words all the orchard trees blossomed  forth in strange colors strangeness had  come into everything growing now  everywhere malignant like tumors  everywhere those hectic and prismatic  variants of some diseased underlying  primary tone without a place among the  known tints of earth  the mental states of the family living  in the area begin to deteriorate  Thaddius went mad in September after a  visit to the well he had gone with a  pail and had come back empty-handed  shrieking and waving his arms and  sometimes lapsing into an inane titter  or a whisper about the moving colors  down there  finally the farmer telling the story and  some other men from a nearby town  witnessed something of cosmic  proportions as the column of unknown  color flared suddenly stronger and began  to weave itself into fantastic  suggestions of shape which each  spectator later described differently  that alien a none dimensioned rainbow of  cryptic poison from the well seething  feeling lapping reaching scintillating  straining and malign Li bubbling in its  cosmic and unrecognizable chromaticism  there burst up from that doomed and a  cursed farm a gleaming Li eruptive  Cataclysm of unnatural sparks and  substance blurring the glance of the few  who saw it and sending forth to the  zenith of embodying cloud bursts of such  colored and fantastic fragments as our  universe must needs to so many stories  about alien encounters seemed oddly  overconfident to me the aliens come as  our peers or as a challenging but  defeatable opponent why is it assumed  that alien life would behave like we do  what did it want I don't think it wanted  anything containing features fundamental  to humanity like desire it's not like us  it's unlike us it's likely because the  stories about recognizable forms are the  easiest stories to tell the ones that  fit into conventional story structure  and reassure audiences of humanity's  self-confidence that it can overcome  whatever the universe can throw at it  but perhaps alien life could be  primarily plant-based or a biology  shifting consciousness that mimics us  perhaps alien life could come in the  form of a space an area in which biology  and physics bend in our primarily  materialistic culture we emphasize that  which can be measured by science and  often reject the idea of that which  cannot it's challenging to portray on  screen the indescribable but film is a  powerful medium and I think annihilation  gives it a valiant effort the rest of  the film is really in service of the end  of the film it is all trying to earn it  really the thing I used to sort of say  is like a kind of soundbite to help  people get their heads around it was  we're gonna go from suburbia to your  psychedelia to help portray the unknown  annihilation draws inspiration from  psychedelic art work and hallucinogenic  drugs experiences on psychedelic drugs  are often talked about by the people  who've had them as indescribable so  taking a page from how users of these  drugs attempt to portray those  experiences make sense  psychedelic imagery is used throughout  the film the heightened sense of beauty  that users of psychedelics report and  the potentially deep expanse of hellish  darkness found in a bad trip are  reflected in the environment of area X  dr. Rick Strassman  in his book DMT the spirit molecule  describes the experiences of volunteers  who were administered dimethyltryptamine  one of the strongest known psychedelic  drugs during a study subjects saw all  sorts of imaginable and unimaginable  things police complex or kaleidoscopic  geometric patterns for example beautiful  colorful pink cobwebs an elongation of  light tremendously intricate tiny  geometric color  like being one inch from a color  television the colors of this imagery  were brighter more intense and deeper  than those of normal awareness or dreams  it was like the blue of a desert sky but  on another planet  the colors were a hundred times deeper  background and foreground distinctions  might merge so that countless images  would occupy a volunteers visual field  it was impossible to tell what was in  front and what was behind many used the  term four-dimensional or beyond  dimensionality to describe this effect  the elements of experience which are  unique aberrant other than average  remain outside the pale of common  language it is precisely these elements  of man's more private experiences that  the literary artist aspires to  communicate for Huxley a science fiction  author who was well versed in the  psychedelic literature was the tool that  was necessary to portray those  subjective inexplicable experiences that  science could not attend to I think film  can play a similar role  in a way the ending of annihilation is a  deus ex machina the term refers to an  old tradition in Greek stage productions  of ending a play by having a God appear  and get the characters out of an  impossible situation an annihilation a  God appears the characters are  travelling towards the center of area X  and towards the end of the story hoping  to find its cause hoping to find an  explanation as the audience so are we  but what do we find when we get there  what explains everything something we  cannot understand the explanation is a  non explanation and this will be  unsatisfying I deserve a better  explanation of the no it's funny doesn't  matter  this is why I think the movie polarizes  the lighthouse sequence 12 minutes long  with no dialogue has to produce that  feeling of all and dread at the sight of  the incomprehensible in the viewer the  viewer will have to feel that this is  the explanation of everything that is  happening and that it is fundamentally  not understandable if they don't feel  that as part of the ending it's likely  the movie will fall flat the washed out  colors and acoustic music of the urban  beginning give way to the vibrant over  saturation and overpowering droning  sense at the end the combination of  visual effects and attempts soundtrack  and sound design make a good effort at  inducing the proper feeling the movies  are subjectively experienced and for  some it won't do the trick the final  shots can be read in two ways you can  see it as shoving the story back in line  with a more conventional narrative the  alien God has been defeated and humanity  has learned how to overcome its own  self-destructive nature or as I see it  the alien God unable to truly be harmed  or defeated by humanity produces its own  Adam and Eve the final stage in this new  life forms gestation hiding now in plain  sight but containing something totally  inhuman  can you describe its form  No  not everyone enjoys films that do more  to provoke and prod than they do to  answer questions and wrap things up but  sometimes in life we face the holy and  explicable and going into the unknown  and coming out alive can be a terrifying  and beautiful experience  it's these images of Heaven and Hell  that a representative of the extremes we  may experience in our lives or afterward  and sometimes we have to be comfortable  with our lack of understanding we may  have to learn to live with our inability  to explain what we experience and what  do you know  [Music]

